body:

#### Question

For studies subject to the NIH Genomic Data Sharing Policy (GDS) (e.g., using NIH funds to generate large-scale human genomic data):
<ol type="a">
  <li>Will you share all large-scale human genomic and associated data in a NIH-designated repository according to the accelerated timelines expected in the GDS Policy?</li>
  <li>Do you anticipate that when sharing you will be able to meet the <a href="https://grants.nih.gov/policy-and-compliance/policy-topics/sharing-policies/gds/institutional-certifications">expectations of the Institutional Certification</a> in the GDS Policy?</li>
</ol>

#### Guidance for Response

A response of "Yes" is expected. If "No" must be responded, provide an explanation in Element 4.

Information about Institutional Certifications for studies involving large-scale human genomic data can be found at the link above.

For repository deposits for this genomic data, NIH-hosted genomic and phenotypic data repositories should be used. For additional information, see [Accessing Genomic Data from NIH Repositories](http://grants.nih.gov/policy-and-compliance/policy-topics/sharing-policies/accessing-data/genomic-data).

